No physical vacuum selection is adopted.

For an even degree-six cubic torus L>=6 put n=|A|=|B|=L^3/2. A P-sector with
m occupied B sites has N=n+m and exactly m/2 minus charges among the n+m
occupied sites, hence m is even. Every such word admits an integer Gauss flow.
At zero cycle angle, every legal four-hop path is a permutation of occupied
charge slots, with a positive coefficient independent of the charge assignment.
Uniformly summing all allowed minus locations therefore gives an exact
occupation isometry. Full colored matrix row sums also equal occupation row
sums, so positive row bounds do not require full-fiber irreducibility.

Use Q=sum C_uv C_uv*, with C_uv* creating an auxiliary unordered B pair D
with multiplicity m_uv(D). This Q is the convention of PRE33; H4=-2Q after
the occupation compression. These auxiliary hard-core variables are only a
combinatorial representation, not a replacement physical instrument.

Let u_m be the normalized uniform superposition of all m-element B subsets.
For one overlapping A pair, define v=sum_D m(D)^2, a=sum_(|D cap D'|=1)
m(D)m(D'), d=sum_(D cap D'=empty)m(D)m(D'), with ordered distinct pairs.
Counting intermediate sets R of size m+2 gives

 <u_m,Q u_m> = [V*C(n-2,m)+A*C(n-3,m-1)+D4*C(n-4,m-2)]/C(n,m),

where V=321n, A=3666n, D4=6624n for L>=6. C(a,b)=0 outside 0<=b<=a.
The local counts are (v,a,d)=(35,390,800) for overlap1 and
(36,416,704) for overlap2, with 3n and6n A pairs respectively.
The m=2 specialization agrees with the independently derived PRE33 formula.

Choose m=n/2, which is even because n=4(L/2)^3. The exact Rayleigh quotient
per n is

 R_half/n = 321(n-2)/(4(n-1)) + 3666n/(8(n-1))
                         +414n(n-2)/((n-1)(n-3))
          =1905/2 +378/(n-1)+414(2n-3)/((n-1)(n-3)) >1905/2.

The root33 local row polynomial extends to arbitrary occupied subsets X.
For an A pair with overlap r=1,2 set sa=|X cap N(a)|, sc=|X cap N(c)|,
t=|X cap N(a) cap N(c)|, na=6-sa,nc=6-sc,ni=r-t,J=na nc-ni.
The occupation row contribution, in the Q convention, is

 P_r=J[(sa+1)(sc+1)-t]+sa ni(nc-1)+sc ni(na-1)+ni(ni-1).

This follows by summing the return multiplicity after every ordered outward
pair: the product of available occupied neighbours is corrected for the
common-neighbour coincidence. It includes returns of pre-existing B records.
